---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-04-14';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for thejohndwilliams.com. What we collect, what we don't, and how to reach us."
>
  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-narrow max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-[10px] sm:text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase opacity-60 mb-3 sm:mb-4">Fine Print</p>
      <h1 class="mb-6 sm:mb-8">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-60 mb-8 sm:mb-12">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-6 text-base sm:text-lg opacity-90 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This is a personal portfolio site. Photography and published work.
          It does not collect personal data for any purpose beyond serving pages.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served through Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare maintains server-side
          request logs (IP address, user agent, URL requested, response code, timestamp)
          for operational and security purposes. These logs are retained per Cloudflare's
          default retention policy and are used only to diagnose traffic anomalies and
          protect the site from abuse. I do not query, export, or aggregate them for
          any other purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, a privacy-first measurement
          tool that collects no personal data, sets no cookies, and does not
          track individual visitors. It measures aggregate page views and
          performance metrics only. No ad networks or tracking pixels run here.
          No cookies are set by the application itself. Your browser may receive
          Cloudflare security cookies (e.g. <code>__cf_bm</code>) which are used to
          distinguish humans from bots and expire after 30 minutes of inactivity.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">What this site does not collect</h2>
        <p>
          No name, email, phone number, or device identifier is collected unless you
          write to me directly. No fingerprinting, session recording, or behavioral
          profiling runs here.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">If you write to me</h2>
        <p>
          Email sent to the contact address on this site is retained in my inbox
          under standard mail-client retention. I do not share it, sell it, or feed
          it into any automated pipeline. If you want your prior correspondence
          deleted, ask and I will.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">Your rights (GDPR / CCPA posture)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are in the EU, UK, or California, you have the right to ask what
          data I hold about you, correct inaccuracies, request deletion, and refuse
          further processing. Given what this site collects — effectively server logs
          and any email you sent me — responding to these requests is straightforward.
          Write to the contact address below.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">AI training</h2>
        <p>
          The photographs on this site are protected intellectual property. The
          <a href="/robots.txt" class="text-cream hover:underline">robots.txt</a>
          explicitly disallows known AI training crawlers from indexing the site.
          If you operate a model-training crawler that honors robots.txt, please do.
          If you use this site's content for model training without permission,
          that is copyright infringement.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif pt-4">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, corrections, or data requests:
          <a href="mailto:jndwcreative@gmail.com" class="text-cream hover:underline">jndwcreative@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="pt-8 text-sm opacity-60">
          This page is written in plain English on purpose. If something here is unclear,
          write to me and I will fix it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
